Checklist

Checklist toward Hoare's 1978 CSP as the lecture slides write it: the language, its translation into Ada, and the slides' programs.

    Language

        Lexical

            - [x] the slides' symbols: → □ ‖ ≠ ≤ ≥ ¬ ∧ ∨
            - [x] ASCII spellings: -> [] | || <> /= <= >=
            - [x] integers, reals, characters, true and false
            - [x] the slides' one-character strings ("A")
            - [x] -- and // comments
            - [x] a hint for Cyrillic look-alike letters

        Processes

            - [x] parallel commands of labeled processes
            - [x] arrays of processes, X(i:1..n)
            - [x] two subscripts, M(i:1..3, j:1..3)
            - [x] families of several definitions, M(i:1..3, 0) and M(i:1..3, j:1..3)
            - [x] fixed subscripts, fac(0)
            - [x] processes defined at the top level, X::*[...]
            - [ ] nested parallel commands

        Declarations and commands

            - [x] integer, real, character and boolean, and the slides' other names
            - [x] arrays with constant bounds, also two-dimensional
            - [x] declarations anywhere in a command list and in guards
            - [x] assignment and tuple assignment
            - [x] skip, blocks
            - [x] alternative and repetitive commands
            - [x] *[ commands ] with no guard
            - [x] constants, and -D NAME=VALUE
            - [x] macros, NAME:: commands, a bracketed body spliced
            - [x] hooks, eat() and print(x), for whatever nothing defines
            - [ ] structured values in variables, x := cons(a, b)
            - [ ] arrays as messages

        Communication

            - [x] output and input of values
            - [x] constructors and signals, has(n), wait()
            - [x] tuples, X!(a, b)
            - [x] array elements as targets, Producer(i)?buffer(in mod 10)
            - [x] integers sent to inputs of reals
            - [x] input guards with conditions and declarations
            - [x] range prefixes anywhere in a guard, s > 0, (i:1..n) X(i)?wait()

        Semantics

            - [x] synchronous communication
            - [x] a random choice among true guards
            - [x] failure of an alternative command whose guards are false
            - [x] distributed termination of repetitive commands
            - [x] failure of a communication with a terminated process
            - [x] deadlock detection

    Translation

            - [x] a task type per family, an entry family per message kind
            - [x] select with unrolled alternatives for input guards
            - [x] Ada names free of reserved words and case clashes
            - [x] the runtime written next to the output
            - [x] --trace, --quiet, --delay, --seed and --timeout

    Examples

            - [x] copy
            - [x] squash, ** into ^
            - [x] semaphore
            - [x] producer and consumer
            - [x] factorial
            - [x] set
            - [x] set with scan
            - [x] set as an array of processes
            - [x] matrix multiplication
            - [x] dining philosophers
            - [x] integral with a bag of tasks
